WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.932
Welcome to Module 7.

00:00:01.932 --> 00:00:07.572
In this module, we are going to build one complete retrieval-augmented generation, or RAG,

00:00:07.572 --> 00:00:08.607
system from beginning to end.

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:15.707
We will use one small student-support knowledge base throughout the module.

00:00:15.707 --> 00:00:20.672
That is important because I do not want the examples to feel disconnected.

00:00:20.672 --> 00:00:25.472
We will start with documents, clean them, split them into chunks, create embeddings,

00:00:25.472 --> 00:00:32.782
retrieve relevant evidence, build a grounded prompt, and finally generate an answer with sources.

00:00:32.782 --> 00:00:37.067
[tts-break] The first goal is not to use as many tools as possible.

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:40.292
The first goal is to understand the architecture.

00:00:40.292 --> 00:00:45.777
Once the simple version works, we will move the same ideas into a vector database and then improve

00:00:45.777 --> 00:00:50.692
retrieval with filtering, keyword search, hybrid search, and reranking.

00:00:50.692 --> 00:00:57.327
By the end, you should be able to take a small document collection from your own work and

00:00:57.327 --> 00:00:59.520
build the same workflow yourself.
